## Context

Child of 1552 (`/replicate` skill). 1552 validates on a development split
(about 10 papers for `assess`, Gavard Scotch plus 2 for `reproduce`) to meet
the 2026-12-05 deadline; this ticket measures the skill on a held-out split
of the I4R corpus afterwards. Not needed for the Toulouse Games.

The corpus: I4R discussion papers, each with the original replication package
and the replicators' reproducibility table, harvested by replicator's dataset
(`replicator dataset fetch --source i4r`, table `replication_results`).

## Design constraints

- Blind the agent to the I4R report; it sees the paper and package only
  (pillage 0266 technique 4, `design/pillage-0266-agentic-reproduction-2026-07-12.md`).
- Include papers published after the evaluated model's training cutoff, and
  report results separately for them (contamination check).
- Held-out split disjoint from 1552's development split, about 30 papers;
  sample stratified by I4R's reproducibility verdict, since the corpus skews
  toward better packages than a reading list.
- `assess`: per-row agreement of the six-row table and ACRe level with I4R's.
  `reproduce`: recall of I4R's discrepancies, on a subset sized to the data
  and compute available. `probe`: coverage of the robustness menu and overlap
  with I4R's choices only, no correctness score.
- Price the run before launching it (author's call above the route cap).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Split, sampling and scoring script committed in replicator (benchmark
      code is replicator's, the skill is the harness's).
- [ ] Results table with per-verb scores, the post-cutoff subset reported
      separately, recorded in replicator and linked from a harness `design/`
      note.
- [ ] Findings that change the skill are fixed in it or ticketed.
